00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.170
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar and you're watching mind your decisions

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.919
Here's a very fun number puzzle

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:14.670
You start out with three identical copies of each number, and you need to make it equal to six

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:20.519
The puzzle is to make each equation true, using common mathematical operations

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.960
There are two rules

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.920
First, you cannot introduce any new digits

00:00:26.439 --> 00:00:32.758
So for example, the operation of cube root would not be allowed, because it involves the digit 3

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:40.379
The second rule is you must have the result equal to 6. You cannot use the not equal symbol.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.340
I thank Tyler Cenko for first

00:00:44.649 --> 00:00:50.519
Suggesting me this problem, and I thank Caio Cerqueira from Brazil for also suggesting it.

00:00:51.129 --> 00:00:57.989
I also want to present a note, my videos will make you so smart that even difficult problems like this will become easy to you

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:00.190
In videos like this you'll see people

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:07.199
Asking for harder problems and it's the best proof that these videos are teaching math to people around the world

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.020
So, can you figure it out?

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:14.970
Give this puzzle a try, and when you're ready, keep watching the video for a solution

00:01:27.909 --> 00:01:29.909
So, how can we solve this puzzle

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:33.689
I will mention that some of the equations have multiple answers

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:39.839
Due to time constraints, I'm only going to present some of the solutions and you may have found another

00:01:40.090 --> 00:01:42.090
creative method to solve one of the equations

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:45.659
Let everyone know your answer in the comments

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:53.759
We'll start solving these by going from some of the more straightforward and easy ones, to then some of the more involved in harder problems

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:57.119
Let's start out with 2 2 2 to equals 6

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:03.030
We can solve this by using the equation 2 plus 2 plus 2 is equal to 6

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.670
So we've already figured out 1

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:13.050
Now 6 6 6 is also similar we can take 6 plus 6 minus 6 to get to 6

00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:17.488
Or we can also do 6 times 6 over 6 is equal to 6

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.499
For our aggregation of solutions. Let's just go with the first equation

00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:31.889
Now let's solve 7 7 7 equals 6 we can do this as 7 minus 7 over 7 is equal to 6

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:41.280
We get a very similar solution for 555 we can take 5 plus 5 over 5 is equal to 6

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.090
So we're making good progress

00:02:45.159 --> 00:02:47.879
Now, let's solve 3 3 3 is equal to 6

00:02:48.819 --> 00:02:54.718
One way to solve this is 3 times 3 minus 3 is equal to 6

00:02:55.810 --> 00:02:58.379
But there are actually several more solutions for this

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:05.000
Another one is 3 factorial plus 3 minus 3 is equal to 6

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:09.920
We can also do 3 factorial times 3 over 3 is equal to 6

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:14.780
Or we can do something like the square root of the quantity

00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:19.769
3 times 3 and then we can add 3 and that's also equal to 6

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:26.819
So for presentation purposes, I'll just take 3 times 3 minus 3 is equal to 6

00:03:28.449 --> 00:03:31.589
Now let's solve 9 9 9 is equal to 6

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:36.840
Well one trick we can use is let's take the square root of each of these 9s

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.900
Here's a handy mathematicians trick.

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:48.080
Since the square root of 9 is equal to 3 we have reduced the problem to solving 3 3 3 is equal to 6

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.140
And this problem has previously been solved

00:03:51.340 --> 00:03:56.310
So any of our solutions for 3 3 3 is equal to 6 will also apply

00:03:56.409 --> 00:04:00.539
To this 9 9 9 once we've applied the square root to each of the 9s

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:06.539
So we could solve this as the square root of 9 times the square root of 9 minus the square root of 9

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:11.219
That's equal to 6 or we take the quantity the square root of 9 factorial

00:04:11.829 --> 00:04:17.519
Plus the square root of 9 minus the square root of 9 is equal to 6 or we have some other solutions

00:04:17.739 --> 00:04:19.509
Like the square root of 9

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:22.288
factorial times 9 over 9 is equal to 6 or

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.279
the quantity

00:04:24.279 --> 00:04:27.200
square root of 9 times the square root of 9 divided by

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:31.960
The square root of nine we take the whole thing and the factorial of that and that is also equal to six

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.740
For presentation purposes. I'll just take this first equation

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:44.080
Now let's go to four for four is equal to six well once again we can take the square root of each of these numbers

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:52.900
again, we have our handy trick since the square root of four is equal 2 we have reduced the problem to 2 2 2 is equal to 6

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:55.200
And that's previously been solved.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:00.040
For example we can take the sum of these numbers and that'll be equal to 6

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:06.460
But if you don't want to do that, you can also do the quantity 4 minus 4 over 4

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.430
And we take the factorial of that quantity

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.809
We can also do the square root of 4 plus 4 over 4

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:19.119
we take that entire quantity and then take the factorial of that and that's also equal to 6, so

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:23.199
for presentation purposes, let's just take this first equation.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.669
Now let's solve 10 10 10 is equal to 6

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.940
Let's do this in steps

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:36.969
We'll do 10 minus 10 over 10, and at this point our result is equal to 9

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:41.920
Well now take the square root of this to get to a result of 3

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:45.189
Then we will take the factorial

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:49.539
So that's how we can get 10 10 10 - equals 6

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.420
Now, what about 1 1 1?

00:05:53.360 --> 00:06:00.849
well notice if we add the 3 numbers we get to 3 and then we'll take the factorial and that's equal to 6 so

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:09.040
Now, how do we solve 0 0 0 is equal to 6? Well first we'll take the factorial of each of these numbers

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.840
We again use a mathematician's trick

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:19.240
Since 0 factorial is equal to 1 we have reduced the problem to 1 1 1 is equal to 6, which has previously been solved.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:25.620
So we add up these numbers and then we take the factorial of the sum and that will be equal to 6

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:34.960
Finally how do we solve 8 8 8 is equal to 6? Many people consider this to be the hardest of all of these equations

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:37.970
So we'll work in steps

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:40.989
We'll take 8 plus 8 and that's equal to 16

00:06:41.510 --> 00:06:45.279
We'll take the square root of that and the square root of 16 is equal to 4

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:49.029
We then take the square root of the square root of that

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:53.890
So the square root of the square root of 16 will be equal to 2

00:06:54.590 --> 00:06:58.270
now we take 8 minus 2 and that's equal to 6

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:00.820
so that's one way to solve this

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:07.940
But another way that you could solve this is you could take 8 plus 8 over 8, and that'll be equal to 9

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:14.890
We then take the square root of 9, which will be equal to 3 and then we take the factorial of 3

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:16.890
and that's equal to 6

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:22.239
So that's it. We figured out how to get 6 in each of these equations

